Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
  "Week 8   Projective Geometry\n",
  StyleBox["Some Algebraic Methods",
    FontSize->18]
}], "Title"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Copyright] Dana Scott 1993/1997/1998",
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["\nNotebook  last edited: ",
    FontSize->16],
  StyleBox["14 October 1998",
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Subtitle",
  FontSize->18],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Doing Algebraic Arguments", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Generation and bases", "Subsection"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Generation by powers", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We have used ",
  StyleBox["monomials",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " extensively as bases, but the polynomials have many other generating sets \
\[LongDash] since a vector space of higher dimension always has many choices \
of bases.  In fact,  ",
  StyleBox["powers",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " are adequate."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Theorem. ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "The linear space ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]\^n\)[u, v, w]\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " of homogeneous ",
  StyleBox["uvw",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "-polynomials of degree ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " is ",
  StyleBox["generated",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " (as a vector space) by the ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th",
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "powers of the ",
  StyleBox["linear",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " polynomials."
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 1]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof:  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "We can see from the proof of the Evaluation Theorem that the expression ",
  StyleBox["PD[f, g]", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[" ", "InlineInput"],
  "cannot vanish on all the ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th powers of linear ",
  StyleBox["uvw-",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "polynomials unless ",
  StyleBox["f", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " is indeed identically zero.   "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Because the two spaces ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]\^n\)[x, y, z]\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]\^n\)[u, v, w]\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "are ",
  StyleBox["dual",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " to each other as vector spaces, this means that the ",
  StyleBox["subspace",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " generated by the ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th powers of the linear polynomials must span the ",
  StyleBox["whole space",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th-degree homogeneous ",
  StyleBox["uvw-",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "polynomials; since, otherwise, there would be an ",
  StyleBox["f", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", not zero, where the expression ",
  StyleBox["PD[f, g]", "InlineInput",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " ",
  StyleBox["did",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " vanish on the subspace.  ",
  StyleBox["Q.E.D.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "As in any vector space, there are many choices of generating sets for the \
space of ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th-degree polynomials, and the proof above does not suggest any ",
  StyleBox["particular",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " basis (being a proof by contradiction).  Here follows a neat proof that \
gives ",
  StyleBox["one",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " maximal array of points in what we might call \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "th-degree\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] ",
  StyleBox["general position",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Theorem. ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "The powers  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\((i\ u + j\ v + w)\)\^n\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ",  where the coefficients run \t\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(i\  = \ 0, 1,  ... \ , n\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  StyleBox[", ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "and",
  StyleBox["  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(j\  = \ 0, 1,  ... \ , i\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ",  \nform an ",
  StyleBox["independent basis",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " for the space  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]\^n\)[u, v, w]\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " of homogeneous ",
  StyleBox["uvw-",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "polynomials of degree  ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "."
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 1]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof:  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox["(by Marko Petkovsek). ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "The points in question form a ",
  StyleBox["triangular array",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " with the property that for each point  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["p",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "  in the array,  there exist  ",
  StyleBox["n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  lines in the plane which together cover all the points of the array ",
  StyleBox["except",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["p",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  ".  These lines are obtained by approaching  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["p",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "  from the outside with lines ",
  StyleBox["parallel",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " to the sides of the triangle. We illustrate this for  ",
  StyleBox["n = 6",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  We need ",
  StyleBox["28",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " points."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Show[
      Graphics[Join[{Hue[1], PointSize[0.05]}, 
          Point/@\(Join@@Table[{i, j}, {i, 0, 6}, {j, 0, i}]\), {
            GrayLevel[0], Point[{3, 1}], Thickness[0.001], 
            Line[{{0, 0}, {6, 0}, {6, 6}, {0, 0}}], Line[{{1, 0}, {6, 5}}], 
            Line[{{4, 0}, {4, 4}}], Line[{{5, 0}, {5, 5}}]}]], 
      AspectRatio \[Rule] Automatic]; \)\)], "Input"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
